ARM: dts: unisoc: rda8810pl-orangepi-i96: enable SDMMC2 for the WiFi SDIO

The RDA5991_G combo chip's data path is SDIO on SDMMC2 (mmc@60000). Its
control interface on i2c1 is already up (patches 15-18) and reports
project_id 0x5991 / chip_version 0x47, so the remaining piece for a
network interface is the SDIO host plus the rdawlan driver.

Board parameters from the vendor tgt_ap_board_config.h: 20 MHz maximum,
mclk inverted, mclk adjust 3. The chip is soldered down, so the host is
non-removable with no card-detect line, and it uses the SDIO interrupt
that rda_mmc already implements (enable_sdio_irq).

Note this only works if the SDMMC2 pads are muxed off the GPIO block:
BB_GPIO_Mode (0x11a09008) bits 15..20 must be clear. u-boot does that in
board_init() -- see recipes-bsp/u-boot/files/rda8810-stage2/board/rda/
rda8810pl/rda_combo.c. There is no RDA pinctrl driver in mainline, so
without the bootloader the host enumerates nothing at all, which looks
exactly like an absent chip. Same trap that hid the I2C1 problem; see
MODEM-WIFI-PORT.md section 10.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board bring-up]

Signed-off-by: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
---

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/rda8810pl-orangepi-i96.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/rda8810pl-orangepi-i96.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/rda8810pl-orangepi-i96.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/rda8810pl-orangepi-i96.dts
@@ -60,6 +60,21 @@
 	rda,mclk-inv;
 };
 
+/*
+ * SDIO to the RDA5991_G WiFi/BT combo. Soldered down: no card detect, never
+ * removed. Vendor board parameters (tgt_ap_board_config.h): 20 MHz, mclk
+ * inverted, mclk adjust 3.
+ */
+&mmc2 {
+	status = "okay";
+	bus-width = <4>;
+	max-frequency = <20000000>;
+	non-removable;
+	cap-sdio-irq;
+	rda,mclk-adj = /bits/ 8 <3>;
+	rda,mclk-inv;
+};
+
 /* Bus 0: hosts the RDA599x WiFi/BT combo control interface. */
 &i2c1 {
 	status = "okay";
